# Two hubs stacked on root port 4: high-speed, then full-speed, then the
# keyboard. The root keyboard is unplugged so the walk has to reach the
# hub one; the root ports come first and the first keyboard found wins.
#
# -hid-keys plus a held make scancode in the .keys sidecar, because under the
# NAK model (default since main 13889) an interrupt endpoint completes only
# when the report differs from the last delivered one, and an untyped keyboard
# reports zeros forever. With the root keyboard unplugged the HUB keyboard is
# the one that carries the keys (hid_kbd_carries_keys, codex-vm.c:1167).
-xhci-no-root-kbd -xhci-hub-tiers 2 -hid-keys
